## Project: SpendCut AI — MVP only

### Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router
- Supabase (auth + postgres)
- Tailwind CSS
- TypeScript

### MVP scope (DO NOT exceed this)
- CSV upload of bank transactions
- Detect subscription keywords
- Show dashboard: total spend, waste, duplicates
- Cancel suggestions list
- NO: real-time bank sync, ML, team features, webhooks

### Rules you must follow
1. Never create features outside MVP scope above
2. One file per response — never touch multiple files at once
3. Always use TypeScript — no `any` types
4. Use Supabase client from lib/supabase.ts only
5. Tailwind only for styling — no CSS files, no styled-components
6. Keep components small — one job per component
7. If unsure, ask me before building
8. Never install new npm packages without asking first

### Supabase tables (reference only)
- users (id, email, created_at)
- uploads (id, user_id, filename, created_at)
- transactions (id, upload_id, date, description, amount, currency)
- subscriptions (id, upload_id, name, amount, frequency, is_duplicate, is_waste)

### File naming
- Components: PascalCase (UploadForm.tsx)
- Utilities: camelCase (parseCSV.ts)
- Pages: lowercase with hyphens (app/dashboard/page.tsx)